WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.435 --> 00:00:03.769
-Well, it looks like
2020 is off to a great start.

00:00:03.769 --> 00:00:05.738
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:05.738 --> 00:00:07.740
[ Theme music plays ]

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:10.844
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.379 --> 00:00:15.815
I'm just [Bleep] with you.
2020 is already the worst.

00:00:15.815 --> 00:00:17.049
[ Laughter ]

00:00:17.049 --> 00:00:18.818
The sky in Australia
is blood red,

00:00:18.818 --> 00:00:20.152
thanks to a climate crisis;

00:00:20.152 --> 00:00:21.987
Republicans are trying to rig
the impeachment trial;

00:00:21.987 --> 00:00:24.157
and the president is threatening
more crimes on Twitter.

00:00:24.157 --> 00:00:26.159
We're less than a week
into 2020.

00:00:26.159 --> 00:00:28.828
The world is like
your friend who tells you

00:00:28.828 --> 00:00:31.864
this is the year he's going to
quit drugs and take up yoga,

00:00:31.864 --> 00:00:33.365
and then, on January 6th,

00:00:33.365 --> 00:00:35.802
you see him trying to
sell his mat for crack.

00:00:35.802 --> 00:00:37.237
[ Laughter ]

00:00:37.237 --> 00:00:39.572
I mean, we should have at least
been able to come together

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:43.376
and enjoy the Patriots getting
knocked out of the playoffs,

00:00:43.376 --> 00:00:45.144
and the first round at home.

00:00:45.144 --> 00:00:47.814
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:47.814 --> 00:00:51.617
I mean, finally, Bill Belichick
was as sad as his outfit.

00:00:51.617 --> 00:00:54.854
For a guy who's supposed to be
good at clock management,

00:00:54.854 --> 00:00:57.924
he always looks like he woke up
five minutes before game time.

00:00:57.924 --> 00:01:00.493
And you know, we couldn't even
take 24 hours

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:01.761
to savor that small victory,

00:01:01.761 --> 00:01:03.462
because the president
spent the weekend

00:01:03.462 --> 00:01:05.064
threatening war crimes
against Iran

00:01:05.064 --> 00:01:08.100
after ordering the assassination
of a top Iranian general

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:10.069
and then, in Orwellian fashion,

00:01:10.069 --> 00:01:12.772
claiming he did it
to stop a war.

00:01:12.772 --> 00:01:13.973
-Breaking news this morning.

00:01:13.973 --> 00:01:16.042
The U.S. has carried out
the assassination

00:01:16.042 --> 00:01:19.212
of a top Iranian military and
intelligence commander.

00:01:19.212 --> 00:01:20.580
The president ordered this.

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:23.616
It was carried out by drone
last night in Iraq.

00:01:23.616 --> 00:01:26.152
-His name was Qasem Soleimani.

00:01:26.152 --> 00:01:28.988
He was Iran's
top military commander.

00:01:28.988 --> 00:01:31.223
-I went to a State Department
briefing today,

00:01:31.223 --> 00:01:33.193
a background briefing,
and the officials basically said

00:01:33.193 --> 00:01:36.796
the ball is in Iran's court, and
we are trying to de-escalate.

00:01:36.796 --> 00:01:40.166
Actually, one official said this
was an act of de-escalation.

00:01:40.166 --> 00:01:44.904
-We took action last night
to stop a war.

00:01:44.904 --> 00:01:49.241
We did not take action
to start a war.

00:01:49.241 --> 00:01:52.245
-Trump thinks we can't accuse
him of rushing into a war

00:01:52.245 --> 00:01:54.847
if he reads his TelePrompTer
super slowly.

00:01:54.847 --> 00:01:56.281
[ Laughter ]

00:01:56.281 --> 00:01:58.785
You can't just kill a top
general of a sovereign nation

00:01:58.785 --> 00:02:00.887
and call it de-escalation.
That's like getting drunk

00:02:00.887 --> 00:02:02.755
and driving your car
into a Kmart

00:02:02.755 --> 00:02:06.092
and then telling the cops,
"I did it to stop my car."

00:02:06.092 --> 00:02:07.426
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.426 --> 00:02:09.929
Trump and his allies are lying
in the exact same ways

00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:12.365
the Bush administration
lied us into a catastrophic war

00:02:12.365 --> 00:02:14.000
in Iraq nearly 17 years ago,

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:15.601
and the exact same people
are doing it.

00:02:15.601 --> 00:02:17.903
After the attack Fox News
decided to turn to

00:02:17.903 --> 00:02:19.472
their stable of
lumpy white guys

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:20.906
who have been wrong
about anything,

00:02:20.906 --> 00:02:23.209
like Lindsey Graham, a champion
of the Iraq war,

00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:25.311
and former Bush officials
and serial liars

00:02:25.311 --> 00:02:26.813
Ari Fleischer and Karl Rove.

00:02:26.813 --> 00:02:28.948
Why are these
the best experts we can get?

00:02:28.948 --> 00:02:31.717
This is like doing a segment
on organizing music festivals

00:02:31.717 --> 00:02:34.353
and interviewing
Billy McFarland and Ja Rule.

00:02:34.353 --> 00:02:38.657
And the same people are
trotting out the same lies

00:02:38.657 --> 00:02:40.927
they did 17 years ago.
For example,

00:02:40.927 --> 00:02:42.528
Vice President Mike Pence lied

00:02:42.528 --> 00:02:45.331
and tried to link Soleimani
to 9/11 in a tweet

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:46.899
that was not supported
by the evidence.

00:02:46.899 --> 00:02:48.601
And if that sounds
familiar to you,

00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:50.569
it's because it's right out of

00:02:50.569 --> 00:02:53.072
the playbook of George W. Bush
and Donald Rumsfeld,

00:02:53.072 --> 00:02:54.674
who repeatedly linked
Saddam Hussein

00:02:54.674 --> 00:02:56.675
to al-Qaeda and
other terrorist groups

00:02:56.675 --> 00:02:58.645
without providing any evidence.

00:02:58.645 --> 00:03:02.047
-The reason I keep insisting
that there was a relationship

00:03:02.047 --> 00:03:04.484
between Iraq and Saddam
and al-Qaeda --

00:03:04.484 --> 00:03:08.554
because there was a relationship
between Iraq and al-Qaeda.

00:03:08.554 --> 00:03:11.424
-There are reports
that there is no evidence

00:03:11.424 --> 00:03:13.893
of a direct link
between Baghdad

00:03:13.893 --> 00:03:16.562
and some of these
terrorist organizations.

00:03:16.562 --> 00:03:22.435
-Reports that say
that something hasn't happened

00:03:22.435 --> 00:03:24.136
are always interesting to me

00:03:24.136 --> 00:03:28.040
because, as we know,
there are known knowns.

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:29.942
There are things
we know we know.

00:03:29.942 --> 00:03:32.277
We also know
there are known unknowns.

00:03:32.277 --> 00:03:35.314
That is to say, we know there
are some things we do not know.

00:03:35.314 --> 00:03:38.484
But there are also
unknown unknowns --

00:03:38.484 --> 00:03:40.786
the ones we don't know
we don't know.

00:03:40.786 --> 00:03:43.256
-Excuse me, but is this
an unknown unknown?

00:03:43.256 --> 00:03:44.791
[ Laughter ]

00:03:44.791 --> 00:03:46.125
-I'm not --
-There are several unknowns --

00:03:46.125 --> 00:03:49.027
-I'm not going to say
which it is.

00:03:49.027 --> 00:03:51.764
-Oh, you're not going to say,
so it's unknown

00:03:51.764 --> 00:03:53.399
whether it's
an unknown unknown.

00:03:53.399 --> 00:03:56.468
But one known that we do know
is what Trump knows,

00:03:56.468 --> 00:03:57.804
which is a known unknown,

00:03:57.804 --> 00:03:59.772
because he un-knows
what he doesn't know.

00:03:59.772 --> 00:04:03.109
Meaning we know
he knows no knowns.

00:04:03.109 --> 00:04:05.278
[ Laughter ]
It's amazing.

00:04:05.278 --> 00:04:06.512
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:06.512 --> 00:04:10.349
It's amazing that we found a way

00:04:10.349 --> 00:04:13.786
to elect people who think
these guys have the right idea.

00:04:13.786 --> 00:04:15.655
It's like if, 17 years from now,

00:04:15.655 --> 00:04:17.690
someone made a movie
called "Cats 2" --

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:19.559
this time with genitals.

00:04:19.559 --> 00:04:21.861
[ Laughter ]

00:04:24.296 --> 00:04:26.999
So, Pence lied, just like
Bush and Rumsfeld lied.

00:04:26.999 --> 00:04:28.867
But, hey, at least
this isn't the first time

00:04:28.867 --> 00:04:30.036
Mike Pence has been wrong

00:04:30.036 --> 00:04:32.137
about a disastrous war
in the Middle East.

00:04:32.137 --> 00:04:33.640
-I am here to report,

00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:37.310
as the United States military
confirmed in Iraq on Monday,

00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:41.614
weapons of mass destruction
have been found in Iraq.

00:04:41.614 --> 00:04:43.449
-It's fitting
that 16 years later,

00:04:43.449 --> 00:04:44.750
Pence is telling the same lies,

00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:47.219
because 16 years later,
he looks the exact same.

00:04:47.219 --> 00:04:49.088
I mean, I'm pretty sure
he's just

00:04:49.088 --> 00:04:51.224
a stock-photo businessman
come to life.

00:04:51.224 --> 00:04:52.659
When he takes off his shirt,

00:04:52.659 --> 00:04:54.826
it says "Getty Images"
across his chest.

00:04:54.826 --> 00:04:56.495
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:56.495 --> 00:04:59.598
So, the Trump administration
tried to link Soleimani to 9/11.

00:04:59.598 --> 00:05:02.535
They also claimed they were
stopping an imminent threat.

00:05:02.535 --> 00:05:04.136
But if that's true,
they haven't presented

00:05:04.136 --> 00:05:07.173
any evidence of that threat
to Congress or the public.

00:05:07.173 --> 00:05:08.507
In fact, a "The New York Times"
reporter tweeted

00:05:08.507 --> 00:05:10.243
that the evidence
for such a threat

00:05:10.243 --> 00:05:12.344
was razor-thin.
And "The times" also wrote

00:05:12.344 --> 00:05:14.580
that national security experts
and even other officials

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:16.181
at the Pentagon
said they were unaware

00:05:16.181 --> 00:05:18.784
of anything drastically new
about Iranian behavior

00:05:18.784 --> 00:05:20.686
in recent weeks.
But that's not good enough

00:05:20.686 --> 00:05:23.256
for "Fox &amp; Friends"
host Ainsley Earhardt,

00:05:23.256 --> 00:05:25.158
who said today that we just
have to trust

00:05:25.158 --> 00:05:27.426
the intelligence agencies.
-So interesting

00:05:27.426 --> 00:05:29.962
that people are critical
of the president's decisions,

00:05:29.962 --> 00:05:32.564
of our intelligence community's
decisions,

00:05:32.564 --> 00:05:34.500
our generals' decisions.
-They want details.

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:36.002
-General Tata said --
Well, they can't have it.

00:05:36.002 --> 00:05:38.104
They can't --
Everything can't be made public.

00:05:38.104 --> 00:05:40.106
We heard Pompeo
over the weekend saying,

00:05:40.106 --> 00:05:42.675
"Everything that we have, the
intelligence community has" --

00:05:42.675 --> 00:05:44.243
he said, "I ran the CIA
at one point.

00:05:44.243 --> 00:05:45.611
We can't release everything.

00:05:45.611 --> 00:05:48.114
We can't release all of our
intelligence information.

00:05:48.114 --> 00:05:49.615
We'll release as much as we can,

00:05:49.615 --> 00:05:51.517
but you just have to
trust us, basically."

00:05:51.517 --> 00:05:53.086
-Oh, we just have to trust them?

00:05:53.086 --> 00:05:55.754
I'm sorry, but I'm not inclined
to trust an administration

00:05:55.754 --> 00:05:57.790
that lies about everything,
even the most dumbest thing.

00:05:57.790 --> 00:06:00.293
Let's not forget, this is
the same guy who literally

00:06:00.293 --> 00:06:04.664
drew a circle on an official
weather map, in Sharpie,

00:06:04.664 --> 00:06:06.932
to claim that Alabama was
going to get hit by a hurricane

00:06:06.932 --> 00:06:09.134
and then pretended he had
no idea how it got there.

00:06:09.134 --> 00:06:11.203
Can you imagine if Trump
actually tries

00:06:11.203 --> 00:06:12.605
to present
some evidence against Iran?

00:06:12.605 --> 00:06:13.740
[ As Trump ]
"I have it right here --

00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:15.107
the top-secret
intelligence briefing

00:06:15.107 --> 00:06:16.642
that proves I was right.

00:06:16.642 --> 00:06:18.845
It says, 'Iran bad,'
right there."

00:06:18.845 --> 00:06:20.846
[ Laughter ]

00:06:20.846 --> 00:06:23.416
"Right there."
[ Applause ]

00:06:23.416 --> 00:06:25.451
[ Normal voice ]
So, there you go.

00:06:25.451 --> 00:06:27.086
You heard "Fox &amp; Friends."

00:06:27.086 --> 00:06:29.521
We have to trust our
intelligence agencies.

00:06:29.521 --> 00:06:32.190
I wonder, though, if she felt
the same way back in May,

00:06:32.190 --> 00:06:34.526
when the intelligence agencies
were investigating Trump.

00:06:34.526 --> 00:06:36.162
What? No, she didn't?

00:06:36.162 --> 00:06:38.097
Oh, and the next clip
proves it?

00:06:38.097 --> 00:06:40.132
Oh, why are you telling me?
You ruined the surprise.

00:06:40.132 --> 00:06:41.701
Alright, well,
let's just show it anyway.

00:06:41.701 --> 00:06:45.504
-There was a Fox News poll,
and folks were asked

00:06:45.504 --> 00:06:48.206
how likely intelligence
agencies, like the FBI,

00:06:48.206 --> 00:06:50.676
broke the law
to investigate President trump.

00:06:50.676 --> 00:06:51.944
Look at that.

00:06:51.944 --> 00:06:55.648
58% said "extremely," "very,"
or "somewhat,"

00:06:55.648 --> 00:06:57.717
and only 31% said "not at all,"
so that just shows you --

00:06:57.717 --> 00:06:59.885
-And you get that number when
you add up the first three.

00:06:59.885 --> 00:07:02.354
-That's pretty scary
that we can't trust the FBI.

00:07:02.354 --> 00:07:04.923
-What?! We can't?

00:07:04.923 --> 00:07:08.361
But that lady on the news
just a second ago said we can!

00:07:08.361 --> 00:07:10.596
[ Laughter ]
Wait a second!

00:07:10.596 --> 00:07:13.632
Oh, my God, one of two things
is happening here.

00:07:13.632 --> 00:07:15.901
Either Trump supporters are
self-serving hypocrites

00:07:15.901 --> 00:07:18.070
who defend intelligence agencies
when they want to bomb

00:07:18.070 --> 00:07:19.438
other countries,
but attack them

00:07:19.438 --> 00:07:21.140
when they investigate
the president's crimes,

00:07:21.140 --> 00:07:24.844
or Ainsley Earhardt
has an evil twin!

00:07:24.844 --> 00:07:26.179
[ Laughter ]

00:07:26.179 --> 00:07:29.215
[ Suspenseful music plays ]

00:07:29.215 --> 00:07:31.317
[ Applause ]

00:07:33.519 --> 00:07:37.389
Now, if you're
a Trump supporter out there,

00:07:37.389 --> 00:07:39.592
claiming anyone who opposes
this act of war

00:07:39.592 --> 00:07:41.226
is siding with the enemy,
let's just remember,

00:07:41.226 --> 00:07:43.695
this is the same president
who literally said

00:07:43.695 --> 00:07:45.531
he and Kim Jong-un,
a brutal dictator

00:07:45.531 --> 00:07:47.633
who starves and tortures
his own people, quote,

00:07:47.633 --> 00:07:50.802
"fell in love because
of Kim's beautiful letters."

00:07:50.802 --> 00:07:53.406
Trump actually said that
about a brutal dictator.

00:07:53.406 --> 00:07:56.508
He sounds like a Southern belle
meeting suitors at a cotillion.

00:07:56.508 --> 00:07:58.644
"My dear Beauregard,
I fell in love with you

00:07:58.644 --> 00:08:01.314
after your beautiful letters."

00:08:01.314 --> 00:08:03.683
[ Laughter ]

00:08:03.683 --> 00:08:05.251
I'm pretty sure most people

00:08:05.251 --> 00:08:07.652
hadn't even heard
Soleimani's name until recently,

00:08:07.652 --> 00:08:10.189
and that includes Trump himself,
who was asked about him

00:08:10.189 --> 00:08:14.593
in a radio interview in 2015 and
clearly had no idea who he was.

00:08:14.593 --> 00:08:16.495
-Are you familiar
with General Soleimani?

00:08:16.495 --> 00:08:21.333
-Yes. Go ahead.
Give me a little.

00:08:21.333 --> 00:08:22.534
Go ahead, tell me.

00:08:22.534 --> 00:08:25.838
-He runs the Quds Forces.
-Yes, okay. Right.

00:08:25.838 --> 00:08:27.740
-Do you expect --
-And I think the Kurds,

00:08:27.740 --> 00:08:30.643
by the way, have been harshly
mistreated by us.

00:08:30.643 --> 00:08:33.178
-No, not the Kurds,
the Quds Forces --

00:08:33.178 --> 00:08:35.247
the Iranian
Revolutionary Guard Quds Forces,

00:08:35.247 --> 00:08:36.649
the bad guys.
-Yes, right.

00:08:36.649 --> 00:08:38.284
-Do you expect his behavior
to change as a result --

00:08:38.284 --> 00:08:39.718
-Oh, I thought you said "Kurds."

00:08:39.718 --> 00:08:42.221
-I love --
I love how Trump tried to

00:08:42.221 --> 00:08:44.957
pretend he knew who he was,
even though he clearly didn't.

00:08:44.957 --> 00:08:46.258
"Do you know General Soleimani?"

00:08:46.258 --> 00:08:48.327
[ As Trump ] Yeah -- No, I do.

00:08:48.327 --> 00:08:51.163
But I want to see
if you know who he is.

00:08:51.163 --> 00:08:53.199
[ Normal voice ]
Clearly, this was

00:08:53.199 --> 00:08:55.033
a reckless act
by an impulsive president

00:08:55.033 --> 00:08:57.369
who hasn't thought through
any of the consequences.

00:08:57.369 --> 00:08:59.137
But a lot of people,
including prominent Democrats,

00:08:59.137 --> 00:09:00.539
are also asking, "Why now?

00:09:00.539 --> 00:09:03.075
Why would a president who's
facing an impeachment trial,

00:09:03.075 --> 00:09:04.576
and mounting evidence
of his guilt

00:09:04.576 --> 00:09:05.811
suddenly start a war with Iran

00:09:05.811 --> 00:09:07.112
as he heads into
an election year.

00:09:07.112 --> 00:09:10.149
I wonder if 2011-2012
Donald Trump

00:09:10.149 --> 00:09:11.517
had anything to say about that

00:09:11.517 --> 00:09:12.985
when it came
to President Obama.

00:09:12.985 --> 00:09:15.187
-I say that he starts
a war in Iran

00:09:15.187 --> 00:09:17.456
before the election,

00:09:17.456 --> 00:09:20.393
which will make it very hard
for the Republican to win, okay?

00:09:20.393 --> 00:09:22.327
And I've said that,
and I predicted that.

00:09:22.327 --> 00:09:24.430
He doesn't talk to anybody.
He'll start a war.

00:09:24.430 --> 00:09:26.398
You know, lives will be wasted
for no reason.

00:09:26.398 --> 00:09:28.100
I happen to think
that the president

00:09:28.100 --> 00:09:30.101
is going to start
a war with Iran.

00:09:30.101 --> 00:09:33.038
I think it will be a short-term
popular thing to do,

00:09:33.038 --> 00:09:35.975
and I think he's going to
do that for political reasons.

00:09:35.975 --> 00:09:39.045
Our president will start
a war with Iran

00:09:39.045 --> 00:09:42.748
because he has absolutely
no ability to negotiate.

00:09:42.748 --> 00:09:46.685
He's weak, and he's ineffective.
So the only way he figures

00:09:46.685 --> 00:09:48.454
that he's going to
get re-elected,

00:09:48.454 --> 00:09:50.423
and as sure
as you're sitting there,

00:09:50.423 --> 00:09:52.558
is to start a war with Iran.

00:09:52.558 --> 00:09:55.227
I believe
that he will attack Iran

00:09:55.227 --> 00:09:58.497
sometime prior to the election
because he thinks

00:09:58.497 --> 00:10:01.299
that's the only way
he can get elected.

00:10:01.299 --> 00:10:04.203
Isn't it pathetic?
-Yes, it is.

00:10:04.203 --> 00:10:07.172
The thing about Trump is
that he never tells the truth

00:10:07.172 --> 00:10:08.474
about himself in the present,

00:10:08.474 --> 00:10:10.709
but he always tells the truth
about himself

00:10:10.709 --> 00:10:12.177
like 10 years in advance.

00:10:12.177 --> 00:10:15.147
When he accuses people of
crossing the border illegally,

00:10:15.147 --> 00:10:17.249
that means, 10 years from now,
he's going to get caught

00:10:17.249 --> 00:10:19.384
climbing over his wall,
trying to flee to Mexico.

00:10:19.384 --> 00:10:23.255
[ As Trump ] David, uh,
why did we make it so tall?

00:10:23.255 --> 00:10:24.456
[ Laughter ]

00:10:24.456 --> 00:10:25.758
[ Normal voice ] So,
it's already terrifying

00:10:25.758 --> 00:10:27.392
that the president is
impulsively lurching

00:10:27.392 --> 00:10:28.961
into an unjust and unmoral war,

00:10:28.961 --> 00:10:31.197
and then, on Sunday,
he decided to go even further

00:10:31.197 --> 00:10:32.898
and threaten war crimes
against Iran

00:10:32.898 --> 00:10:35.601
with a truly psychotic tweet
that he genuinely thought

00:10:35.601 --> 00:10:37.937
counted as some sort of
official legal document.

00:10:37.937 --> 00:10:39.237
Here is the very real tweet

00:10:39.237 --> 00:10:40.606
the president
of the United States

00:10:40.606 --> 00:10:41.974
sent out on Sunday.

00:10:41.974 --> 00:10:44.577
"These media posts
will serve as notification

00:10:44.577 --> 00:10:46.412
to the United States Congress
that should Iran

00:10:46.412 --> 00:10:48.246
strike any
U.S. person or target,

00:10:48.246 --> 00:10:50.449
the United States will quickly
and fully strike back

00:10:50.449 --> 00:10:52.484
and perhaps in a
disproportionate manner.

00:10:52.484 --> 00:10:54.320
Such legal notice
is not required

00:10:54.320 --> 00:10:56.421
but is given nevertheless."
That's right.

00:10:56.421 --> 00:10:58.824
The same guy who brought you
such tweets as,

00:10:58.824 --> 00:11:00.993
"Robert Pattinson
should dump Kristen Stewart,"

00:11:00.993 --> 00:11:04.496
and, "I have never seen a thin
person drinking diet Coke,"

00:11:04.496 --> 00:11:06.399
now thinks his tweets

00:11:06.399 --> 00:11:09.201
serve as official
legal notice to Congress.

00:11:09.201 --> 00:11:10.936
I don't think this tweet counts

00:11:10.936 --> 00:11:13.138
as legal notice to commit
an act of war,

00:11:13.138 --> 00:11:14.440
but I do think it counts

00:11:14.440 --> 00:11:16.041
as legal notice
to have you committed.

00:11:16.041 --> 00:11:17.642
That tweet sounds like something

00:11:17.642 --> 00:11:20.045
that could be scrawled
on the walls of a psych ward.

00:11:20.045 --> 00:11:21.980
"Let this serve
as a legal notice

00:11:21.980 --> 00:11:24.082
that I know you're hiding pills
in my applesauce,

00:11:24.082 --> 00:11:27.352
and I will find them
and sue you for malpractice."

00:11:27.352 --> 00:11:29.655
[ Applause ]
And by the way,

00:11:29.655 --> 00:11:33.325
threatening a disproportionate
response is a war crime,

00:11:33.325 --> 00:11:35.327
just like when Trump tweeted
the previous day

00:11:35.327 --> 00:11:37.897
that, "If Iran strikes any
Americans or American assets,

00:11:37.897 --> 00:11:40.131
we have targeted
52 Iranian sites,

00:11:40.131 --> 00:11:41.534
some at a very high level

00:11:41.534 --> 00:11:43.768
and important to Iran
and the Iranian culture.

00:11:43.768 --> 00:11:45.771
And those targets
and Iran itself

00:11:45.771 --> 00:11:48.306
will be hit
very fast and very hard."

00:11:48.306 --> 00:11:49.875
First of all,
it's not reassuring

00:11:49.875 --> 00:11:52.077
when the president tweets
in all caps like a lunatic

00:11:52.077 --> 00:11:54.312
who sees his ex-girlfriend
posting pictures

00:11:54.312 --> 00:11:56.648
of herself with another guy,
and texts her at 3:00 a.m.,

00:11:56.648 --> 00:11:58.350
"Who is Brad?
Why are you in Cabo?

00:11:58.350 --> 00:12:02.020
I will hit him
very fast and very hard!"

00:12:02.020 --> 00:12:04.923
A war with Iran would be
unjust and immoral,

00:12:04.923 --> 00:12:06.158
cause mass death and suffering,

00:12:06.158 --> 00:12:08.027
and destabilize
the region and the world.

00:12:08.027 --> 00:12:09.461
And Trump obviously
hasn't thought about,

00:12:09.461 --> 00:12:11.129
or doesn't care about,
those consequences,

00:12:11.129 --> 00:12:12.464
because, by all accounts,

00:12:12.464 --> 00:12:14.333
he made this decision
impulsively,

00:12:14.333 --> 00:12:16.435
to the surprise of his own
top military officials.

00:12:16.435 --> 00:12:18.170
"The New York Times" reported
that they were stunned,

00:12:18.170 --> 00:12:20.439
flabbergasted, and alarmed
when trump chose

00:12:20.439 --> 00:12:22.541
the option of killing Soleimani.

00:12:22.541 --> 00:12:24.109
Apparently,
Trump's military advisers

00:12:24.109 --> 00:12:25.878
put the option
on one PowerPoint slide

00:12:25.878 --> 00:12:28.214
to make the other options
seem more reasonable,

00:12:28.214 --> 00:12:30.482
not actually thinking
he would pick it.

00:12:30.482 --> 00:12:32.284
One briefing slide
shown to Trump

00:12:32.284 --> 00:12:34.886
listed several follow-up steps
the U.S. could take,

00:12:34.886 --> 00:12:36.388
among them targeting Soleimani.

00:12:36.388 --> 00:12:38.657
Unexpectedly,
Trump chose that option.

00:12:38.657 --> 00:12:42.027
Oh, oh, did Donald Trump
do the unexpected...

00:12:42.027 --> 00:12:44.229
[ Laughter ]
...instead of the reasonable?

00:12:44.229 --> 00:12:46.732
Did you guys
not get a briefing on him?

00:12:46.732 --> 00:12:49.367
You can't expect
the reasonable choice

00:12:49.367 --> 00:12:51.870
from the guy who
stared into a eclipse,

00:12:51.870 --> 00:12:54.640
and when his umbrella
got caught,

00:12:54.640 --> 00:12:56.541
just left it on the stairs.

00:12:56.541 --> 00:12:58.511
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:12:58.511 --> 00:13:00.779
Congress must do
everything in its power

00:13:00.779 --> 00:13:03.081
to stop an unjust and immoral
war with Iran

00:13:03.081 --> 00:13:04.950
that will have
disastrous consequences.

00:13:04.950 --> 00:13:07.152
That's why thousands of
protesters took to the streets

00:13:07.152 --> 00:13:09.121
over the weekend
in cities across the country

00:13:09.121 --> 00:13:11.123
to say no to war with Iran.

00:13:11.123 --> 00:13:12.691
We have an impulsive, lawless
president

00:13:12.691 --> 00:13:14.092
threatening war crimes,

00:13:14.092 --> 00:13:16.862
who thinks his tweets count
as official legal documents.

00:13:16.862 --> 00:13:19.164
You got to ask...
-Isn't it pathetic?

00:13:19.164 --> 00:13:21.266
-This has been
"A Closer Look."

00:13:21.266 --> 00:13:24.236
[ Theme music plays ]

